  "configuration_id": "config_047",
  "reason": "Evidence: The two multiprofile experiments (config_002: scvi_n200+avgpool+concat=0.6315, config_003: pca_n2000+avgpool+concat=0.6186) show a large ~10-point gain over singleprofile, but both use avgpool aggregation and concat fusion. We have zero evidence about whether transformer aggregation could further improve multiprofile performance by modeling inter-profile interactions rather than simple averaging. Question: This experiment isolates the effect of aggregation (avgpool→transformer) while holding all other variables constant at the best-performing config_002 settings (scvi_n200, resnet50, concat). Why this is the best next step: Aggregation is the most architecturally consequential untested dimension in the multiprofile setting—avgpool discards profile-specific information that a transformer could preserve and re-weight. A single-variable change from the current best config cleanly attributes any performance shift to the aggregation mechanism, and the result will determine whether further investment in more complex aggregation (or in fusion) is warranted under the limited budget."
}

